<title>SWITZERLAND: UBS sees Roche headed for Sfr 12,100.</title>
<headline>UBS sees Roche headed for Sfr 12,100.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland said it saw Roche Holding AG non-voting equity certificates headed for 12,100 Swiss francs by the end of the year and upgraded its earnings forecast slightly.</p>
<p>UBS, which rates Roche a buy, said the 11 percent 1996 sales growth announced by the company was in line with projections. &quot;On the basis of long-term profit potential, we see a price target of 12,100 francs by the end of the year,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>It gave these forecasts in a research report:</p>
<p>	     Net (million Sfr)  EPS   P/E   Dividend   Yield</p>
<p> 1995	  3,372	  391   27.9    64	  0.59 pct</p>
<p> 1996E	 3,877	  449   24.3    76	  0.70</p>
<p> 1997E	 4,450	  516   21.2    88	  0.81</p>
<p> 1998E	 5,190	  602   18.1   100	  0.92</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
